Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 13:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] runsc/boot: wire DST components into loader and kernel

All previous patches defined DST types, constructors, and getters but
never wired them together. Two things were missing:

  1. pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_init.go - adds Kernel.InitDST which sets all
     unexported dst* fields (only settable from within the kernel package)
     and starts the deterministic scheduler goroutine.

  2. runsc/boot/loader.go - in Loader.New, after the timekeeper is set
     up, calls newDSTClocks() so virtual time is used when DST is enabled,
     then constructs and installs all DST subsystems (RNG, scheduler,
     snapshot tree, syscall-fault table) via Kernel.InitDST, and finally
     calls initDSTControlSocket so the control server is listening before
     any container tasks are created.
---
 pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_init.go | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 runsc/boot/loader.go          | 16 ++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_init.go

